			"Message": "chore(Cargo): Exclude additional build directory from workspace\n\nSigned-off-by: Nikola Hristov <Nikola@PlayForm.Cloud>",
			"SHA": "a95e0e4b355b28cb4b2487b5c6ec632fde1a5bc1"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-05T05:20:34Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				116,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Synchronize Cocoon build artifacts and Wind service catalogs\n\nUpdate the Element submodule to align build artifacts with the recent PascalCase refactoring in the Cocoon extension host. The `Target/` directory is regenerated to reflect the decomposition of `Window/Namespace` into dedicated factory modules (OutputChannel, StatusBar, Terminal, Webview), ensuring import paths match the strict directory hierarchy.\n\nConcurrently, bump the `CommandCatalogVersion` and `ServiceCatalogVersion` constants in the Wind UI service submodule. This maintains consistency between the runtime service registry and the latest upstream state, covering 544 commands and 483 services without altering the API surface.\n\nThese changes guarantee build stability across the extension host and UI layers, preventing runtime discrepancies between source and bundled artifacts.",
			"SHA": "629967d2db90eedcea217021770e86f59d843a10"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-05T05:12:45Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				116,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Modularize UI bridge into dedicated installers\n\nUpdate the Element submodule to decompose the monolithic Bridge.ts in Sky into domain-specific installer modules (InstallDebug, InstallTasksAndDecorations). This refactoring isolates logic for debug lifecycle, custom editors, workspace edits, and batched UI decorations.\n\nThe new structure utilizes dynamic imports to reduce static dependency graphs and improve tree-shaking while strictly adhering to the PascalCase directory hierarchy. Concurrently synchronize the SideCar submodule to align the native backend with the updated frontend event relays.\n\nThese changes advance the strategic decomposition of the UI workbench, enabling finer-grained maintenance and a cleaner separation of concerns between the Mountain backend and Sky frontend.",
			"SHA": "834271eee0266a9e93ccf73298a14bd70c397a4e"
		}
	],
